          "text": "Added the cheapest available Electronics item to the cart: 'USB-C Charging Cable 6ft' by CableTech, $7.99.\n\nEvidence chain:\n1. Category: opened the Electronics listing from the home page (category=Electronics, 50 results); the product page breadcrumb reads Home > Electronics > Chargers & Power Adapters.\n2. Cheapest: set Sort by = 'Price: Low to High'. The page-order price list read $7.99, $7.99, $7.99, $7.99, then $15.00, $15.00, $15.00, $15.00, $15.00, $15.00, $17.99, $18.82. So the minimum price in Electronics is $7.99 and no cheaper item exists in the 50 results. Two of the more expensive items were marked 'Currently unavailable' and were excluded, so the cheapest AVAILABLE item is still $7.99.\n3. Selected item: the plain 'USB-C Charging Cable 6ft' among the four $7.99 cables, because it showed the strongest availability signals (In Stock, 1,727 ratings, 1700+ bought in past month, sold by Amazon.com).\n4. Membership: prepare_link_membership was called before the change (baseline 0 matching links for product_320). After adding, verify_link_membership returned status 'new_link_membership_observed' with matching_links 0 -> 1. The cart page independently shows 'USB-C Charging Cable 6ft', Qty 1, price 7.99, Subtotal 7.99, and the header badge reads 1 item.\n\nCaveats I am stating rather than hiding:\n- The $7.99 minimum is a four-way tie (Refurbished, 2-Pack, Pro Edition, plain 6ft). The task requirement 'cheapest item' is met on price; there is no single uniquely cheapest product.\n- The membership witness only proves the chosen entity appears in the cart view. Price minimality rests on the sorted listing and the visible cart price, not on the witness.\n- Add to Cart silently did nothing twice: it showed an 'Added to Cart' panel while the cart stayed empty. It only persisted once the Qty select was explicitly set to 1. Anyone reproducing this should set the quantity first."
